# DAX Measures

## Revenue & Profitability

```DAX
Total Sales =
SUM(Orders[Sales])
```

```DAX
Total Profit =
SUM(Orders[Profit])
```

```DAX
Profit Margin % =
DIVIDE([Total Profit],[Total Sales])
```

Purpose:
Measures overall business profitability.

---

## Customer Analysis

```DAX
Customer Count =
DISTINCTCOUNT(Orders[Customer ID])
```

```DAX
Total Orders =
DISTINCTCOUNT(Orders[Order ID])
```

```DAX
Average Order Value =
DIVIDE([Total Sales],[Total Orders])
```

Purpose:
Analyzes customer activity and purchasing behavior.

---

## Category Analysis Using CALCULATE

### Technology Sales

```DAX
Technology Sales =
CALCULATE(
    [Total Sales],
    Orders[Category] = "Technology"
)
```

### Technology Profit

```DAX
Technology Profit =
CALCULATE(
    [Total Profit],
    Orders[Category] = "Technology"
)
```

### Technology Profit Margin

```DAX
Technology Profit Margin =
DIVIDE(
    [Technology Profit],
    [Technology Sales]
)
```

Purpose:
Evaluates financial performance of Technology products.

---

## Returns Analysis

```DAX
Returned Orders =
COUNTROWS(Returns)
```

```DAX
Return Rate % =
DIVIDE(
    [Returned Orders],
    [Total Orders]
)
```

Purpose:
Tracks operational performance and customer returns.

---

## Time Intelligence

### Previous Year Sales

```DAX
Previous Year Sales =
CALCULATE(
    [Total Sales],
    DATEADD(
        Orders[Order Date],
        -1,
        YEAR
    )
)
```

### Year over Year Growth

```DAX
YoY Growth % =
DIVIDE(
    [Total Sales] - [Previous Year Sales],
    [Previous Year Sales]
)
```

### Running Sales

```DAX
Running Sales =
CALCULATE(
    [Total Sales],
    FILTER(
        ALL(Orders[Order Date]),
        Orders[Order Date] <= MAX(Orders[Order Date])
    )
)
```

Purpose:
Measures business growth and sales trends over time.

